/* ============================================================================
determinant-2x2.epher -- the 2x2 determinant, formula and builtin cross-check

The determinant of [[a, b], [c, d]] is ad - bc; it is zero exactly when
the rows are proportional and the matrix is singular (any linear algebra
text, e.g. Strang, "Introduction to Linear Algebra", 5th ed., sec. 5.1).
The classroom formula is written out for teaching; the built-in det gives
the same number, and each result is checked against it. All exact.

Run it from a terminal:
  Linux (deb, rpm):  epher /usr/lib/epher/scripts/algebra/matrices/determinant-2x2.epher
  Windows:           epher "$env:LOCALAPPDATA\epher\scripts\algebra\matrices\determinant-2x2.epher"
  macOS:             epher /Applications/epher.app/Contents/Resources/scripts/algebra/matrices/determinant-2x2.epher

The knobs to edit are the matrices A and B below.
============================================================================ */

// ---- the knobs ---------------------------------------------------------------
const A = [[3, 7], [2, -4]]
const B = [[2, 3], [4, 6]]         // rows proportional: singular

// ---- helpers -----------------------------------------------------------------
def cdet(a, b, c, d) = a * d - b * c      // classroom formula; builtin: det

// ---- results -----------------------------------------------------------------
print("det A by formula:", cdet(A[1][1], A[1][2], A[2][1], A[2][2]))
print("det A by builtin:", det(A))
print("they agree:", cdet(A[1][1], A[1][2], A[2][1], A[2][2]) == det(A))
print("det B by formula:", cdet(B[1][1], B[1][2], B[2][1], B[2][2]))
print("they agree:", cdet(B[1][1], B[1][2], B[2][1], B[2][2]) == det(B))
/* ---- expected output ----
= [[3, 7], [2, -4]]
= [[2, 3], [4, 6]]
= det A by formula: -26
= det A by builtin: -26
= they agree: true
= det B by formula: 0
= they agree: true
*/
